# Test: a discard entry with the default direction and protocol commits beside a
# policy-based peer with the default icmp-error-check, while a bypass entry that
# carries ICMP errors in clear to the same peer's remote selectors is still refused.
# Spec: plan/release/fixes/spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps.md (AC-19, D-6).
#
# Question: does the ike plugin's offline verifier, reached through `ze config
# validate`, accept the default discard entry beside a default peer? A unit test
# (rfc4301_icmp_overlap_test.go) decides verifyICMPOverlap alone; only the CLI run
# proves the whole verify (validateIPsecSections: the SPD order, the implicit
# discard and the ICMP overlap steps together) accepts what an operator types.
#
# VALIDATES:
#   seq=1 `vpn ipsec policy drop-host` (action discard, no direction, so both; no
#         protocol, so any) under `unmatched discard`, beside peer `site` with no
#         icmp-error-check leaf (default true) and no `vti bind`, validates with
#         exit 0. Ze's kernel honours the discard for ICMP arriving on the peer's
#         SA (K1, XFRM_ZE_CAP_ICMP_REVERSE), so no refusal applies.
#   seq=2 the control: the same configuration with `vpn ipsec policy icmp-out`
#         (bypass, direction out, protocol 1, remote 10.2.0.0/16) is refused with
#         refusal A's text, so seq=1's exit 0 is the verifier answering, not a
#         verifier that never ran.
# PREVENTS: the commit refusal of a default discard beside a default peer
#   (refuseICMPCheckDiscard, removed) coming back, and a verify that tells the
#   operator to turn the Section 6.2 check off to get a working discard.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE: that the entry drops traffic. The packet half is
# TestRFC4301NonErrorICMPOutsideSelectorsIsDiscarded
# (internal/component/ike/dataplane/rfc4301_icmp_nonerror_integration_linux_test.go).
#
# The entry's prefixes are disjoint from the peer's selectors, so the SPD order
# refusal (equal order on overlapping selectors, engine/spd_order.go) cannot
# answer; refusal B refused an inbound ICMP-matching discard whatever its prefixes.
#
# RED PROOF: restore refuseICMPCheckDiscard and its call in verifyICMPOverlap
# (engine/icmp_overlap.go, as at HEAD before the D-6 change): seq=1 exits 1 naming
# `vpn ipsec policy drop-host`, red. Delete the refuseICMPErrorBypass call: seq=2
# exits 0, red.
#
# Every cmd asserts its own exit with exit=. Needles carry no ':'.

stdin=discard:terminator=EOF_DISCARD
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched discard
		policy drop-host {
			action discard
			local {
				prefix 0.0.0.0/0
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.51.100.0/24
			}
		}
		esp-group esp-default {
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		ike-group ike-default {
			proposal 1 {
				dh-group 14
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer site {
				ike-group ike-default
				esp-group esp-default
				local-address 10.0.0.1
				remote-address 10.0.0.2
				mode tunnel
				traffic-selector 1 {
					local {
						prefix 10.1.0.0/16
					}
					remote {
						prefix 10.2.0.0/16
					}
				}
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_DISCARD

stdin=bypass:terminator=EOF_BYPASS
vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched discard
		policy drop-host {
			action discard
			local {
				prefix 0.0.0.0/0
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.51.100.0/24
			}
		}
		policy icmp-out {
			action bypass
			direction out
			protocol 1
			local {
				prefix 0.0.0.0/0
			}
			remote {
				prefix 10.2.0.0/16
			}
		}
		esp-group esp-default {
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		ike-group ike-default {
			proposal 1 {
				dh-group 14
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer site {
				ike-group ike-default
				esp-group esp-default
				local-address 10.0.0.1
				remote-address 10.0.0.2
				mode tunnel
				traffic-selector 1 {
					local {
						prefix 10.1.0.0/16
					}
					remote {
						prefix 10.2.0.0/16
					}
				}
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_BYPASS

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=discard:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
reject=stdout:contains=drop-host
reject=stdout:contains=icmp-error-check false

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=bypass:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=vpn ipsec policy icmp-out
expect=stdout:contains=carries ICMP errors in clear to the peer's remote selectors
reject=stdout:contains=`vpn ipsec policy drop-host`
